COUNTED from the outcome lines of the dev_reflow2 hub's trial log, Session 5 (the report behind art:dev-reflow2-two-agent-exercise-feedback-2026-09-29). Five triage agents each ran root-cause per issue, fetched fresh, against reflow2 0.74.0 and flo2.

THE REPORTER'S CONCLUSIONS, 30 issues (I25 and I29 are one finding; I30 was found during the triage). The reporter was the hub session itself: Claude, writing from a designer agent's friction log.
- WHOLLY OVERTURNED, 6:
  - I2: "three inconsistent gates" was one flo2 gateway rule;
  - I5: flo2, not reflow2, refused the oversized reply;
  - I8: the "none describes themselves" statement was true, since it counts people only;
  - I11: a cure existed (contains under the Project);
  - I13: CAUSES is excluded from the walk on purpose, and GOVERNED_BY threads;
  - I21: the auth enum already encodes it.
- PARTLY OVERTURNED, 5:
  - I1: the approval is incomplete, not false;
  - I9: an Actor consumer already clears it through create_edge;
  - I14: record_finding does write a dated measurement;
  - I18: the path total is computed, but the verdict uses the sum;
  - I24: create_edges was reachable through the connector.
- REFRAMED, 1: I20. reflow2 declares none of its derived relations, so there is nothing for a tool to evaluate.
- WORKING AS DESIGNED, 1: I27.
That is 12 of 30 changed by measurement.

RECURRENCES, 7 of 30. Each cause had been root-caused in an earlier session and was still live on 0.74.0:
- I2's fixed "lands proposed" hint: a defect of 2026-08-14;
- I3's stale "OPEN" names: flo2 F12, fixed 2026-09-19 for the body only;
- I12, parks never named: the 4th instance of its class;
- I14a, the bare VERIFIES refusal: root-caused 2026-09-28;
- I16, related_to dropped: first seen 2026-09-23, root-caused 2026-09-28;
- I19, a run has one status: root-caused 2026-09-28;
- I30, record_finding writes defaults on revise: root-caused 2026-09-28.
Six of the seven were found again within 1 to 10 days of their root cause.

WHAT THIS IS EVIDENCE FOR, stated as observation, not cause:
(a) The skill-driven triage earns its cost: reading the report would have carried 12 wrong or partial conclusions into the design, and the reporter was the maintainer's own agent.
(b) A root cause recorded without its fix leaves the class live, and a later report re-finds it. On 2026-09-29 Anthony answered this triage with "Fix all the root causes"; the fix program is epoch:fix-what-the-two-agent-exercise-found-2026-09-29.

LIMITS:
- Counted from one-line outcome summaries written by the hub session from each agent's report, not re-derived from every fact.
- "Partly" is a judgement per item.
- The 30 items come from one exercise and one reporter.
